1
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
The extraordinary true story of Solomon Northup.

2
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:02,000
12 Years a Slave is a drama, history film directed by Steve McQueen.

3
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:30,000
In the pre-Civil War United States, Solomon Northup, a free black man
from upstate New York, is abducted and sold into slavery.

4
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Facing cruelty as well as unexpected kindnesses Solomon struggles
not only to stay alive, but to retain his dignity.

5
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:26,000
In the twelfth year of his unforgettable odyssey, Solomon’s chance meeting
with a Canadian abolitionist will forever alter his life.

6
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Solomon Northup, played by Chiwetel Ejiofor.

7
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Edwin Epps, played by Michael Fassbender.

8
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Patsey, played by Lupita Nyong'o.

9
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:18,000
William Ford, played by Benedict Cumberbatch.

10
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:46,000
John Tibeats, played by Paul Dano.

11
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Mary Epps, played by Sarah Paulson.

12
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:42,000
12 Years a Slave is a 2013 biographical historical drama film directed by Steve McQueen from a screenplay by John Ridley, based on  the
1853 slave memoir Twelve Years a Slave by Solomon Northup, an American of mixed race, who was kidnapped from Washington, D.C.

13
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:10,000
by two conmen in 1841 and sold into slavery.

14
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:38,000
He was put to work on plantations in the state of
Louisiana for 12 years before being released.

15
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
The first scholarly edition of David Wilson's version of Northup's story
was co-edited in 1968 by Sue Eakin and Joseph Logsdon.

16
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
In the film, Chiwetel Ejiofor stars as Solomon Northup.

17
01:15:56,000 --> 01:16:02,000
Supporting roles are portrayed by Michael Fassbender, Benedict Cumberbatch, Paul Dano, Garret Dillahunt, Paul Giamatti, Scoot
McNairy, Lupita Nyong'o, Adepero Oduye, Sarah Paulson, Brad Pitt, Michael Kenneth Williams, and Alfre Woodard.

18
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:30,000
Principal photography took place in New Orleans,
Louisiana, from June 27 to August 13, 2012.

19
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:58,000
The locations used were four historic antebellum plantations:
Felicity, Bocage, Destrehan, and Magnolia.

20
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
Of the four, Magnolia is nearest to the actual
plantation where Northup was held.

21
01:33:48,000 --> 01:33:54,000
12 Years a Slave received widespread critical acclaim and was named the
best film of 2013 by several media outlets and critics.

22
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:22,000
It earned over $187 million on a production budget of $22 million.

23
01:42:44,000 --> 01:42:50,000
The film received nine Academy Award nominations, winning for Best Picture, Best
Adapted Screenplay for Ridley, and Best Supporting Actress for Nyong'o.

24
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
The Best Picture win made McQueen the first black British producer to ever receive the
award and the first black British director of a Best Picture winner.

25
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:46,000
The film was awarded the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Drama, and the British Academy of Film and
Television Arts recognized it with the BAFTA Awards for Best Film and Best Actor for Ejiofor.

26
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:14,000
Since its release, the film has been cited as among the best of the 2010s, the 21st century, and of all time, with it being named the 44th greatest film since
2000 in a BBC poll of 177 critics in 2016 and the 51st best film of the 21st century in a New York Times poll of over 500 filmmakers in 2025.

27
02:00:36,000 --> 02:00:42,000
In 2023, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically or aesthetically
significant", making it the ninth film designated in its first year of eligibility, the 49th Best Picture Academy Award winner and the most recently released film to be selected.

28
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:10,000
The film explores themes of slavery, plantation, based on memoir
or autobiography, violin player, physical abuse.

29
02:09:32,000 --> 02:09:38,000
The tone is emotional.
